        "faq": [
          {
            "q": "Is SnapDock free?",
            "a": "Right now, yes, for a limited time. SnapDock becomes a paid app after launch. Everyone who gets it while it's free is an early adopter and gets every future update free, for life."
          },
          {
            "q": "Does it work with my theme?",
            "a": "Yes. The dock and title bars recolour themselves whenever you switch Omarchy themes."
          },
          {
            "q": "Will it mess up my setup?",
            "a": "No. SnapDock 2 never edits your own settings files. It adds one line to Hyprland's settings and keeps everything else in its own folders. Coming from an older SnapDock? It first puts back everything the old version changed."
          },
          {
            "q": "How do I switch between Mac and Windows style?",
            "a": "Click the gear on the dock (SnapDock Settings). Dock style is at the bottom: Mac, Windows or SnapDock. It changes right away."
          },
          {
            "q": "How do I move the icons on the dock?",
            "a": "Right-click the dock and choose Unlock to move icons (or use the switch in SnapDock Settings). The icons wiggle: drag them where you want them, then lock the dock again."
          },
          {
            "q": "An app froze. How do I close it?",
            "a": "Right-click its icon on the dock and choose Force quit. Or press Ctrl + Shift + Esc for the Task Manager, pick the app and press Force quit."
          },
          {
            "q": "Where does a minimized window go?",
            "a": "It waits out of sight, and its icon stays in the dock. Click the icon and it comes back on the desktop it came from, in the same spot. To bring every minimized window back at once: SnapDock \u2192 Snap layouts \u2192 Bring back all minimized windows."
          },
          {
            "q": "What are the desktops 1 2 3 4 5?",
            "a": "The numbers at the top left of Omarchy are separate desktops, each with its own windows (like Task View desktops on Windows). Click a number to switch to it. SnapDock lets you send a window to one: \u29c9 on the title bar, or drag the window onto the tiles that appear at the top left."
          },
          {
            "q": "Something isn't working. What do I do?",
            "a": "Open a terminal and type snapdock doctor. It checks the usual causes (another dock running, a settings error, a missing program) and tells you what to do."
          },
          {
            "q": "How do I update it?",
            "a": "The Omarchy Store's Updates tab shows new versions: press UPDATE."
          },
          {
            "q": "How do I remove it?",
            "a": "Press Remove on SnapDock's page in the Omarchy Store. Or open a terminal and type snapdock uninstall. It takes out its one line and its own files, and your setup is exactly as it was."
          },
          {
            "q": "Which Omarchy do I need?",
            "a": "A recent Omarchy (version 4 or newer). On older versions SnapDock tells you to update Omarchy first and changes nothing."
          }
        ],
